                    {
                        "form_id": "ce5166d6-c021-4ccb-a853-c07cb7bda5f3",
                        "entry_id": "be08f062-1419-30ac-a6aa-d0c5bd54f09f",
                        "tags": [
                            "future"
                        ],
                        "form": "буду/будешь… прихлёбывать"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "44614315-bc20-39a0-83e7-c69b74844f96",
                        "entry_id": "be08f062-1419-30ac-a6aa-d0c5bd54f09f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "разг. пить небольшими глотка́ми"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b5203f35-174b-40f8-a8ed-dcd7f78d3b4b",
                                "sense_id": "44614315-bc20-39a0-83e7-c69b74844f96",
                                "text": "Разговор сделался порядочнее, и я заметил, что большая часть крикунов обратилась к одному молодому малорослому человеку, который с важностию курил трубку и прихлёбывал пунш."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1aade0bf-160a-47ba-a36f-4ea140d3593f",
                                "sense_id": "44614315-bc20-39a0-83e7-c69b74844f96",
                                "text": "Пока большинство российских болельщиков глушили с горя водку и придумывали обидные анекдоты, которые, скорее всего, не дойдут до американцев, семья молодых юристов сидела у телевизора, нервно прихлёбывала кофе и спорила, кто же виноват в нашем всенародном позоре."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "77d8a0dc-658e-409f-b668-83c63a7c94f5",
                        "source_entry_id": "be08f062-1419-30ac-a6aa-d0c5bd54f09f",
                        "source_sense_id": "44614315-bc20-39a0-83e7-c69b74844f96",
                        "target_lang_word": "sip",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "sip",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6ad670d6-e83f-3889-8e24-f14509d14e2d",
                                        "entry_id": "c81432c3-114f-3dde-8d58-d1f54f8937d1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A small mouthful of drink"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "aae78c81-14f7-3483-83fa-3d4e743a0932",
                                        "entry_id": "c81432c3-114f-3dde-8d58-d1f54f8937d1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An event at which people drink alcohol in small, usually sub-intoxicating amounts."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "032f0ece-304d-414e-b623-17e500a1d78d",
                                                "sense_id": "aae78c81-14f7-3483-83fa-3d4e743a0932",
                                                "text": "Earl is always a good time. His appearance at parties, whether it's a smart cocktail sip or a basement gig, is mandatory."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "sip",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bb055a1a-39c6-3886-a664-84d6e68c6939",
                                        "entry_id": "59f58eb5-b993-3ce6-b864-cb96eb113f51",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To drink slowly, small mouthfuls at a time."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "877298a1-01f5-4628-ba03-2b60acd9f3c8",
                                                "sense_id": "bb055a1a-39c6-3886-a664-84d6e68c6939",
                                                "text": "He held out to me a bowl of steaming broth, that filled the room with a savour sweeter, ten thousand times, to me than every rose and lily of the world; yet would not let me drink it at a gulp, but made me sip it with a spoon like any baby."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ce6dcc2c-ca1a-4283-988b-9008ebe7b9a0",
                                                "sense_id": "bb055a1a-39c6-3886-a664-84d6e68c6939",
                                                "text": "A waiter brought his aperitif, which was a small scotch and soda, and as he sipped it gratefully he sighed."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6a6071e0-e63a-44e3-8132-d6e58a04ed7a",
                                                "sense_id": "bb055a1a-39c6-3886-a664-84d6e68c6939",
                                                "text": "bright young things in jeans and T-shirts huddle around laptops, sipping lattes or munching on free food."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "843666e0-61fa-3b28-a68b-00a708e19fd3",
                                        "entry_id": "59f58eb5-b993-3ce6-b864-cb96eb113f51",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To drink a small quantity."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "06c41bf7-df3f-448d-b8bb-4a52db9f4c3e",
                                                "sense_id": "843666e0-61fa-3b28-a68b-00a708e19fd3",
                                                "text": "[She] rais'd it to her mouth with sober grace; / Then, sipping, offered to the next in place."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "65121192-424c-31d4-b588-24bce6dfbea7",
                                        "entry_id": "59f58eb5-b993-3ce6-b864-cb96eb113f51",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To taste the liquor of; to drink out of."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "edaee708-df5f-4fd3-8423-8af44177a32c",
                                                "sense_id": "65121192-424c-31d4-b588-24bce6dfbea7",
                                                "text": "They skim the floods, and sip the purple flowers."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "346f30a0-5bf9-3603-adf4-d2170d6af242",
                                        "entry_id": "59f58eb5-b993-3ce6-b864-cb96eb113f51",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alternative form of seep."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Scotland",
                                            "US",
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "alternative",
                                            "dated"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "dc5463ff-fef9-329b-9987-2db843605c2d",
                                        "entry_id": "59f58eb5-b993-3ce6-b864-cb96eb113f51",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To consume slowly."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a81283ea-566f-45bb-a3f9-da58b88a59c0",
                                                "sense_id": "dc5463ff-fef9-329b-9987-2db843605c2d",
                                                "text": "Sales of lightbulbs which sip electricity, and whose increased cost in the shops is easily paid for over their lifetime, used to double every year; in 1990/1991, they leapt sevenfold."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "99451b69-ee9f-4abb-b8e0-e6e0622e150c",
                                                "sense_id": "dc5463ff-fef9-329b-9987-2db843605c2d",
                                                "text": "It makes a small car, the Chevy Cobalt, which sips petrol in moderation and is therefore selling well."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bf5f8d7b-432b-4d25-a645-8ad12db7d9eb",
                                                "sense_id": "dc5463ff-fef9-329b-9987-2db843605c2d",
                                                "text": "Even when turned off, these devices can idly sip electricity from your outlet costing you money."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
